INSERT INTO posts (title, slug, author, cover_url, body_md, published, published_at, created_by_email) VALUES ('SOMETHING FISHY...', 'something-fishy', '@grandpa', NULL, '<p><em><u>The&nbsp;Flying&nbsp;Kicks</u></em></p><p>I&nbsp;remember&nbsp;during&nbsp;my&nbsp;River&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;source&nbsp;days.&nbsp;The&nbsp;great&nbsp;Chief&nbsp;Odero&nbsp;Gogni&nbsp;or&nbsp;who&nbsp;was&nbsp;it?&nbsp;Sitting&nbsp;in&nbsp;his&nbsp;hut,&nbsp;swallowing&nbsp;from&nbsp;his&nbsp;Goat&nbsp;Wife&nbsp;Akoko&nbsp;like&nbsp;nobody&#39;s&nbsp;business&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;suddenly&nbsp;paap!&nbsp;He&nbsp;dies&nbsp;from&nbsp;choking.</p><p></p><p>How&nbsp;can&nbsp;you&nbsp;be&nbsp;choked&nbsp;by&nbsp;fish&nbsp;and&nbsp;die?&nbsp;Was&nbsp;it&nbsp;the&nbsp;author&nbsp;who&nbsp;just&nbsp;wanted&nbsp;to&nbsp;kill&nbsp;all&nbsp;the&nbsp;men&nbsp;in&nbsp;her&nbsp;novel?&nbsp;Like&nbsp;these&nbsp;men&nbsp;really&nbsp;died&nbsp;weird&nbsp;deaths&nbsp;baana.</p><p></p><p>We&#39;re&nbsp;just&nbsp;outside&nbsp;playing,&nbsp;yes&nbsp;those&nbsp;days&nbsp;as&nbsp;kids&nbsp;ladies&nbsp;and&nbsp;gentlemen.&nbsp;Playing&nbsp;the&nbsp;famous&nbsp;banoo,&nbsp;gen&nbsp;alpha&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;born&nbsp;taos&nbsp;will&nbsp;never&nbsp;relate&nbsp;to&nbsp;this.</p><p></p><p>&quot;Woooi,&nbsp;majirani!&nbsp;Saidieniiii!!&quot;&nbsp;Comes&nbsp;a&nbsp;voice&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;neighborhood.&nbsp;Yeah,&nbsp;we&nbsp;were&nbsp;also&nbsp;neighbors&nbsp;right?&nbsp;We&nbsp;rush&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;scene,&nbsp;not&nbsp;to&nbsp;offer&nbsp;help&nbsp;but&nbsp;to&nbsp;see&nbsp;for&nbsp;ourselves&nbsp;what&nbsp;was&nbsp;going&nbsp;on.</p><p></p><p>The&nbsp;scene&nbsp;was&nbsp;devastating&nbsp;ladies&nbsp;and&nbsp;gentlemen,&nbsp;our&nbsp;brother&nbsp;was&nbsp;laying&nbsp;there,&nbsp;not&nbsp;our&nbsp;brother&nbsp;per&nbsp;say&nbsp;let&#39;s&nbsp;just&nbsp;call&nbsp;him&nbsp;that.&nbsp;Eeeish,&nbsp;holding&nbsp;his&nbsp;neck&nbsp;wriggling&nbsp;with&nbsp;pain.</p><p></p><p>&quot;Amenyongwa&nbsp;na&nbsp;mfupa&nbsp;ya&nbsp;samaki,&quot;&nbsp;his&nbsp;goat&nbsp;wife&nbsp;says.&nbsp;Chief&nbsp;Odero&nbsp;Gogni&nbsp;started&nbsp;like&nbsp;this.&nbsp;Eeeei,&nbsp;the&nbsp;scene&nbsp;makes&nbsp;me&nbsp;remember&nbsp;what&nbsp;happened&nbsp;in&nbsp;that&nbsp;River&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;Source&nbsp;book.</p><p></p><p>He&nbsp;is&nbsp;given&nbsp;lots&nbsp;of&nbsp;ugali&nbsp;to&nbsp;push&nbsp;that&nbsp;thing&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;stomach.&nbsp;Seems&nbsp;to&nbsp;me&nbsp;that&nbsp;wueh!,&nbsp;the&nbsp;bone&nbsp;was&nbsp;really&nbsp;strong,&nbsp;I&nbsp;mean&nbsp;it&nbsp;endured&nbsp;that&nbsp;force,&nbsp;the&nbsp;guy&nbsp;continued&nbsp;choking,&nbsp;his&nbsp;face&nbsp;almost&nbsp;turning&nbsp;pale.&nbsp;Struggling&nbsp;to&nbsp;speak.</p><p></p><p>&quot;Boom!&quot;&nbsp;This&nbsp;wasn&#39;t&nbsp;a&nbsp;bomb&nbsp;or&nbsp;something,&nbsp;it&nbsp;was&nbsp;strong&nbsp;kick&nbsp;landing&nbsp;on&nbsp;his&nbsp;back.&nbsp;Thank&nbsp;God&nbsp;he&nbsp;was&nbsp;strong,&nbsp;he&nbsp;would&nbsp;have&nbsp;broken&nbsp;some&nbsp;few&nbsp;bones.&nbsp;Pieces&nbsp;of&nbsp;ugali&nbsp;get&nbsp;dislodged&nbsp;from&nbsp;wherever&nbsp;they&nbsp;were&nbsp;stuck.&nbsp;The&nbsp;fish&nbsp;bone&nbsp;was&nbsp;still&nbsp;intact.&nbsp;It&nbsp;was&nbsp;like,&nbsp;&quot;Kaneva&nbsp;be&nbsp;me.&quot;</p><p></p><p>All&nbsp;the&nbsp;efforts&nbsp;appeared&nbsp;to&nbsp;be&nbsp;futile,&nbsp;things&nbsp;were&nbsp;worsening,&nbsp;it&nbsp;was&nbsp;partial&nbsp;choking&nbsp;so&nbsp;he&nbsp;had&nbsp;some&nbsp;chances,&nbsp;small&nbsp;chances&nbsp;to&nbsp;cough.&nbsp;Guess&nbsp;what?&nbsp;I&nbsp;also&nbsp;don&#39;t&nbsp;know&nbsp;what&nbsp;was&nbsp;happening.</p><p></p><p>The&nbsp;nduthi&nbsp;guy&nbsp;had&nbsp;just&nbsp;arrived&nbsp;right&nbsp;on&nbsp;time,&nbsp;things&nbsp;were&nbsp;not&nbsp;getting&nbsp;easy&nbsp;any&nbsp;time.&nbsp;He&nbsp;was&nbsp;rushed&nbsp;to&nbsp;hospital,&nbsp;the&nbsp;nearest&nbsp;hospital&nbsp;was&nbsp;like&nbsp;4km&nbsp;away.</p><p></p><p>What&nbsp;happened&nbsp;next?&nbsp;They&nbsp;did&nbsp;a&nbsp;surgery&nbsp;on&nbsp;him&nbsp;because&nbsp;the&nbsp;stubborn&nbsp;bone&nbsp;decided&nbsp;to&nbsp;make&nbsp;the&nbsp;next&nbsp;its&nbsp;permanent&nbsp;residence.&nbsp;It&nbsp;had&nbsp;affected&nbsp;the&nbsp;guy&nbsp;so&nbsp;much,&nbsp;the&nbsp;ugali&nbsp;effect,&nbsp;yes,&nbsp;the&nbsp;swallowing&nbsp;made&nbsp;the&nbsp;bone&nbsp;tear&nbsp;some&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;internal&nbsp;organs&nbsp;a&nbsp;lil&nbsp;bit.</p><p></p><p>He&nbsp;was&nbsp;almost&nbsp;dying.</p><p></p><p>Hey&nbsp;guys,&nbsp;the&nbsp;first&nbsp;of&nbsp;fish&nbsp;bone&nbsp;choking&nbsp;is&nbsp;not&nbsp;adding&nbsp;other&nbsp;factors&nbsp;to&nbsp;choking&nbsp;like&nbsp;Hot&nbsp;ugali.&nbsp;You&nbsp;will&nbsp;kill&nbsp;someone&nbsp;some&nbsp;day.</p><p></p><p>Anyways....that&nbsp;was&nbsp;a&nbsp;fishy&nbsp;incident</p>', TRUE, '2026-07-24T08:59:06.343Z', 'simiyu@seresponse.org');
INSERT INTO posts (title, slug, author, cover_url, body_md, published, published_at, created_by_email) VALUES ('More than a walk in the park', 'more-than-a-walk-in-the-park', 'Granpa', NULL, '<p></p><p>When many people think of a picnic, they imagine baskets full of food, laughter, music, and games. While those moments are certainly part of the experience, a Scouts Emergency Response (SER) picnic is something much more meaningful.</p><p></p><p>For us, every picnic is an opportunity to learn, grow, and prepare to save lives.</p><p></p><p>Where Recreation Meets Preparedness</p><p></p><p>Scouts Emergency Response organizes team-building picnics at different parks and recreational sites, creating an environment where members can relax, connect, and strengthen friendships. However, what makes our picnics unique is that they double as practical first aid learning experiences.</p><p></p><p>Instead of spending the entire day enjoying food and games, members participate in realistic first aid scenarios carefully designed to simulate emergencies that could happen in everyday life. From managing unconscious casualties and treating severe bleeding to responding to fractures, choking incidents, and other emergencies, participants are challenged to think critically and apply the skills they have learned during training.</p><p></p><p>These practical exercises transform ordinary parks into outdoor classrooms where confidence is built through action.</p><p>Learning by Doing</p><p></p><p>First aid is a practical skill. Reading about it or watching demonstrations is important, but confidence only comes from practice.</p><p></p><p>During our picnics, members work together in teams to assess scenes, perform primary and secondary surveys, provide appropriate first aid, and communicate effectively during emergency situations. These simulations help participants sharpen their decision-making, teamwork, leadership, and communication skills while reinforcing the importance of remaining calm under pressure.</p><p></p><p>Because the scenarios are conducted in open public spaces, they also expose members to the kinds of environments where real emergencies often occur.</p><p></p><p>Building Stronger Teams</p><p></p><p>Beyond the simulations, the picnics provide an opportunity for members to build stronger relationships. Sharing meals, organizing potluck activities, playing outdoor games, and spending time together creates trust and camaraderie that later translates into better teamwork during emergency responses.</p><p></p><p>Emergency response is rarely an individual effort. It depends on people working together efficiently, and these informal interactions help build the unity needed when responding to real incidents.</p><p></p><p>Part of a Bigger Mission</p><p></p><p>The Scouts Emergency Response mission is simple but powerful: to equip young people with essential first aid knowledge and practical emergency response skills that can save lives.</p><p></p><p>Our picnics are just one of the many ways we achieve this mission. They complement our broader training programs, which include:</p><p></p><p>* Physical first aid training sessions</p><p>* Online learning and webinars</p><p>* Practical first aid simulations</p><p>* Community outreach and awareness programs</p><p>* Team-building exercises and educational picnics</p><p></p><p>Together, these activities ensure that learning never stops and that our members remain ready to respond whenever emergencies arise.</p><p></p><p>Every Outing is an Opportunity</p><p></p><p>For Scouts Emergency Response, a picnic is never just about the destination or the food. It is an opportunity to refresh our minds, strengthen our friendships, and most importantly, practice the skills that could one day save someone&#39;s life.</p><p></p><p>We believe that preparedness should be continuous, engaging, and accessible. By combining recreation with realistic first aid practice, we create memorable experiences that develop competent, confident, and compassionate young responders.</p><p></p><p>Because when emergencies happen, it is not enough to know first aid—you must be ready to use it.</p><p></p>', TRUE, '2026-08-09T14:19:39.788Z', 'sia.elvis@seresponse.org');
